    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nI wrote a `mail.json` snippet file that caused the following error upon any completion:\n\n```\nE5108: Error executing lua vim/shared.lua:0: s: expected string, got nil\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'error'\n        vim/shared.lua: in function 'validate'\n        vim/shared.lua: in function 'trim'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2533: in function 'get_comment_leaders'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2514: in function 'get_indent'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:2041: in function 'session_init'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1308: in function 'call_in_insert_mode'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1306: in function 'insert'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1690: in function 'call_in_insert_mode'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1682: in function 'insert'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:1153: in function 'select'\n        /home/shuber/.vim/plugged/mini.nvim/lua/mini/snippets.lua:798: in function 'expand'\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n```\n\nThe underlying reason is that in `H.get_comment_leaders()` in `lua/mini/snippets.lua` fails if `comment_part` happens to be an empty string (or would not contain a \":\").\n\n### Reproduction\n\nOpen `mail.json` a snippet file and add an arbitrary entry. Open a `example.eml` and try the completion out. There is a chance that the plugin `https://gitlab.com/dbeniamine/vim-mail` actually causes the comments string to be pathological; I have not tested.",
