            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> The underlying reason is that in `H.get_comment_leaders()` in `lua/mini/snippets.lua` fails if `comment_part` happens to be an empty string (or would not contain a \":\").\n\nCan you, please, show the actual value of the `'comments'` option which gives this error? I was able to reproduce empty part with something like `':#,'` (i.e. trailing `,` makes it look like there is an empty string part), but this seems to be a Neovim/Vim bug and this value should not be allowed. Setting entry for 'comments' without `:` results in the error as they *must* contain `:` (see `:h format-comments`).",
