        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> s1:/*,mb:*,ex:*/,://,b:#,:%,:XCOMM,n:>,fb:-,fb:•,n:|,\n> And I found the bad line in my own config files. I am sorry.\n\nNo worries. But yeah, the trailing comma should not be there. Removing it should make everything work.\n\n> Still, it might be worth merging the sanitizing code anyways as it would make the plugin more robust?\n\nNormally, I'd agree. But this is a relatively rare case, which should not exist, and should *be able* to exist. So I don't think it is a good idea here, as adding a guard for something like this feels... wrong somehow :) I'd open an issue in vim/vim about trailing commas in 'comments' even being allowed.\n\nClosing as not really an issue with 'mini.snippets', as it assumes a documented behavior while non-documented behavior can and should be addressed on the user side.",
